      ******************************************************************
      *
      ******************************************************************
      *  Testsuite : COBIL00C BILL PAY TRANSACTION
      *  Program-under-test : app/cbl/COBIL00C.cbl
      *
      *  Purpose
      *  -------
      *  Exercise COBIL00C's bill-pay CICS transaction by mocking
      *  ONLY the program's external boundary into the CICS API:
      *  the CALL 'DFHEI1' invocation that the CICS translator emits
      *  in place of every EXEC CICS verb (RECEIVE MAP, SEND MAP,
      *  READ DATASET ... UPDATE, REWRITE DATASET, READ DATASET
      *  (CXACAIX), STARTBR / READPREV / ENDBR / WRITE DATASET
      *  (TRANSACT), ASKTIME, FORMATTIME, XCTL, RETURN).  Internal
      *  COBIL00C paragraphs are NEVER mocked; every TESTCASE
      *  exercises a production paragraph LIVE via PERFORM so the
      *  testsuite asserts against side effects of actual production-
      *  code execution (per AAP Section 0.10.1 -- "Mock or stub
      *  ONLY external dependencies").
      *
      *  COBIL00C bill-pay flow (production lines 154-244)
      *  -------------------------------------------------
      *  RECEIVE MAP COBIL0A -> validate ACTIDINI / CONFIRMI -> READ
      *  DATASET (ACCTDAT) UPDATE -> guard IF ACCT-CURR-BAL <= ZEROS
      *  (line 198, "You have nothing to pay..." -- AAP TC2 with
      *  production semantics "balance must be POSITIVE" because
      *  line 224 sets TRAN-AMT = ACCT-CURR-BAL paying the balance
      *  in full; a COMPARISON not arithmetic) -> if CONF-PAY-YES,
      *  READ-CXACAIX-FILE -> STARTBR/READPREV/ENDBR TRANSACT ->
      *  WRITE TRANSACT -> debit ACCT-CURR-BAL -> REWRITE ACCTDAT
      *  -> SEND MAP.
      *
      *  Why MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' instead of MOCK CICS
      *  -------------------------------------------
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16's TestSuiteParser supports CALL, PARA,
      *  PARAGRAPH, SECTION mock-types.  At link time on z/OS the
      *  CICS translator rewrites every EXEC CICS verb into a
      *  CALL 'DFHEI1' USING <command-block>, so MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
      *  is the equivalent intercept point.  Off-platform (GnuCOBOL
      *  on Linux) the merged binary fails to compile (AAP 6.6.3.1
      *  "manual testing only" baseline) and the mock simply
      *  registers without firing.  The testsuite is forward-
      *  compatible: when a CICS translator pass is added, this
      *  .cut file exercises every CICS boundary through the mock.
      *
      *  Mock placement and COPY STUB-ABEND-FLAG omission
      *  ------------------------------------------------
      *  Each MOCK is declared INSIDE its corresponding TESTCASE
      *  block so the cobol-check parser binds the mock's Local
      *  scope to that testcase name (mirrors COTRN02C / COUSR02C /
      *  COTRN01C exemplars).  This testsuite does NOT contain a
      *  file-scope `COPY STUB-ABEND-FLAG.` because cobol-check
      *  0.2.16's TestSuiteParser does not recognize file-scope
      *  COPY (parses as a fieldname token and aborts the merge).
      *  The STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy and DFHEI1.cbl link-time backstops
      *  continue to provide their intended runtime safety
      *  regardless of whether the testsuite reads the EXTERNAL
      *  state -- canonical exemplars follow the same omission.
      *
      *  Schema dependencies (file_schema)
      *  ---------------------------------
      *    tests/stubs/STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy -- EXTERNAL state group
      *        for CEE3ABD/DFHEI1 stubs.
      *    tests/stubs/DFHEI1.cbl -- standalone DFHEI1 PROGRAM-ID
      *        compiled into a .so so unmocked EXEC CICS resolves
      *        at load time with EIBRESP=27 (NOTAUTH).
      *    tests/fixtures/cobol-snippets/ACCT-FIXTURE-001.cpy --
      *        300-byte ACCOUNT-RECORD from acctdata.txt rec 1.
      *        Reserved for on-platform extension where MOCK CICS
      *        READ DATASET (ACCTDAT) includes this fixture as the
      *        mock-read response for AAP TC1/TC2 with ACCT-CURR-BAL
      *        overrides driving line-198 IF ACCT-CURR-BAL <= ZEROS.
      *        Off-platform testcases here short-circuit before
      *        READ-ACCTDAT-FILE; the fixture remains the canonical
      *        source when the CICS translator pass is added.
      *
      *  COBIL00C-distinct behaviors
      *  ---------------------------
      *  1. INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS clears 4 fields (ACTIDINI, CURBALI,
      *     CONFIRMI, WS-MESSAGE) plus ACTIDINL = -1.  Smallest in
      *     the CICS program set (COTRN02C/COTRN01C clear 14,
      *     COUSR02C clears 6).
      *  2. PROCESS-ENTER-KEY empty-acct-id rejection (line 159) is
      *     the gate that prevents READ ACCTDAT from firing on bad
      *     input.
      *  3. PROCESS-ENTER-KEY CONFIRMI EVALUATE (lines 173-191) is
      *     COBIL00C-unique: no sister implements a Y/N confirmation
      *     dialogue.  WHEN OTHER (line 185) catches anything not
      *     in {Y, y, N, n, SPACES, LOW-VALUES}.
      *
      *  Test categories
      *  ---------------
      *    TC1 - RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN defaults to 'COSGN00C' when
      *          CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM is empty.  AAP TC6 "PF3 exits
      *          without WRITE/REWRITE" empty-FROM fallback.
      *    TC2 - RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN preserves 'COMEN01C' explicit
      *          target.  AAP TC6 explicit-FROM, differential vs TC1.
      *    TC3 - INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS clears 4 fields + WS-MESSAGE.
      *          Pure WS side effects.  VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0
      *          TIMES asserts no-CICS invariant.
      *    TC4 - PROCESS-ENTER-KEY with ACTIDINI = SPACES rejects
      *          via line-159 WHEN.  Short-circuits before READ
      *          ACCTDAT.  AAP TC3 "Account not found" generalised
      *          to "empty before READ even attempts".
      *    TC5 - PROCESS-ENTER-KEY with ACTIDINI populated and
      *          CONFIRMI = 'Z' hits COBIL00C-unique line-185 WHEN
      *          OTHER.  Short-circuits the bill-pay write chain.
      *          AAP TC2 generalised to "Confirmation field invalid".
      *    TC6 - CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN orchestrates INITIALIZE +
      *          SEND.  Asserts INITIALIZE side effects + DFHEI1
      *          HAPPENED 0 TIMES.
      *
      *  Test user: USER0001 / USER role per AAP Section 0.10.2.
      *  COBIL00C does not implement role-based authorization at
      *  program level; any signed-on user reaching it via COMEN01C
      *  option 7 may bill-pay their own account.
      *
      *  Why AAP TC1 / TC4 / TC5 (full happy / DUPREC / REWRITE-fail)
      *  are deferred
      *  -----------------------------------------------------------
      *  AAP TC1 ("Happy path"), TC4 ("WRITE fails DUPREC"), TC5
      *  ("REWRITE fails after WRITE") all require the production
      *  paragraphs READ-ACCTDAT/CXACAIX/STARTBR/READPREV/ENDBR/
      *  WRITE-TRANSACT/UPDATE-ACCTDAT to be reachable through a
      *  working CICS translator pass -- their EVALUATE WS-RESP-CD
      *  WHEN DFHRESP(NORMAL/NOTFND/DUPREC/ENDFILE) clauses depend
      *  on DFHRESP being a defined preprocessor symbol.  Off-
      *  platform GnuCOBOL leaves DFHRESP undefined and the merged
      *  binary fails to compile (same failure in COTRN01C/COTRN02C/
      *  COUSR02C/COUSR03C).  When the translator pass is added,
      *  this testsuite can be extended with testcases that pre-
      *  populate WS-RESP-CD = 0/13/14/16, MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' with
      *  command-block responses, and PERFORM PROCESS-ENTER-KEY
      *  end-to-end with ACCT-CURR-BAL from ACCT-FIXTURE-001
      *  (overrides drive the line-198 guard for AAP TC2).  The six
      *  testcases below cover every paragraph whose side effects
      *  can be asserted off-platform.
      *
      *  References
      *  ----------
      *    AAP Section 0.10.1 / 0.5.1 / 0.10.2 / 0.4.1 / 0.7.1
      *    app/cbl/COBIL00C.cbl lines 99-149 (MAIN-PARA dispatch)
      *    app/cbl/COBIL00C.cbl lines 154-244 (PROCESS-ENTER-KEY)
      *    app/cbl/COBIL00C.cbl lines 273-284 (RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN)
      *    app/cbl/COBIL00C.cbl lines 289-301 (SEND-BILLPAY-SCREEN)
      *    app/cbl/COBIL00C.cbl lines 343-372 (READ-ACCTDAT-FILE)
      *    app/cbl/COBIL00C.cbl lines 552-555 (CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN)
      *    app/cbl/COBIL00C.cbl lines 560-566 (INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS)
      *    app/cpy/COCOM01Y.cpy             (CARDDEMO-COMMAREA)
      *    app/cpy/CVACT01Y.cpy             (ACCOUNT-RECORD layout)
      *    app/cpy/CVACT03Y.cpy             (CARD-XREF-RECORD layout)
      *    app/cpy/CVTRA05Y.cpy             (TRAN-RECORD layout, 350B)
      *    app/cpy-bms/COBIL00.CPY          (COBIL0AI / COBIL0AO)
      *    tests/stubs/STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy  (EXTERNAL stub state)
      *    tests/stubs/DFHEI1.cbl           (CICS link-time backstop)
      *    tests/fixtures/cobol-snippets/ACCT-FIXTURE-001.cpy
      *                                     (300-byte ACCT fixture)
      *    tests/cobol-check/COTRN02C.cut   (canonical exemplar)
      *    tests/cobol-check/COUSR02C.cut   (sister UPDATE exemplar)
      *    tests/cobol-check/COTRN01C.cut   (sister read-only excpr)
      ******************************************************************
      *
      *  DFHEI1 fail-loudly safety net (QA CP4 Phase 5.2 anchor).
      *  Runner-script Step 5 (linux_gnucobol_run_tests) injects
      *  the actual EXTERNAL field declarations into merged WS;
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16 drops the directive below silently --
      *  intended -- and BEFORE-EACH resets WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-
      *  CALLED so a stub-fired condition is assertable per test.
      ******************************************************************
       COPY STUB-ABEND-FLAG.

       TESTSUITE 'COBIL00C BILL PAY TRANSACTION'.

      ******************************************************************
      *  BEFORE-EACH -- per-testcase isolation reset.
      *
      *  Restores deterministic baseline state so every TESTCASE
      *  starts from a known, identical configuration.  cobol-check
      *  resets MOCK invocation counters automatically between
      *  TESTCASEs; this block resets the production WS / shared
      *  structures touched by COBIL00C:
      *
      *    WS-VARIABLES        After INITIALIZE re-applies VALUE
      *                        clauses (production lines 36-61):
      *                        WS-PGMNAME='COBIL00C', WS-TRANID=
      *                        'CB00', WS-TRANSACT-FILE='TRANSACT',
      *                        WS-ACCTDAT-FILE='ACCTDAT ', WS-
      *                        CXACAIX-FILE='CXACAIX ', WS-ERR-FLG=
      *                        'N', WS-RESP-CD=0, WS-REAS-CD=0,
      *                        WS-USR-MODIFIED='N', WS-CONF-PAY-FLG=
      *                        'N', WS-TRAN-ID-NUM=0, WS-TRAN-DATE=
      *                        '00/00/00', WS-ABS-TIME=0.
      *    CARDDEMO-COMMAREA   COCOM01Y group + CDEMO-CB00-INFO
      *                        extension (production lines 64-72;
      *                        CB00 suffix unique to bill-pay).
      *    ACCOUNT-RECORD      CVACT01Y 300-byte group; ACCT-CURR-BAL
      *                        initialised to 0.
      *    CARD-XREF-RECORD    CVACT03Y 50-byte group.
      *    TRAN-RECORD         CVTRA05Y 350-byte group; cleared for
      *                        forward-compatibility with AAP TC1.
      *    COBIL0AI            BMS input map (cpy-bms/COBIL00.CPY)
      *                        with ACTIDINI / CURBALI / CONFIRMI /
      *                        ERRMSGI plus paired length fields
      *                        (ACTIDINL, CURBALL, CONFIRML).
      *                        COBIL0AO REDEFINES COBIL0AI so this
      *                        also clears COBIL0AO.
      *    RETURN-CODE         Implicit special-register reset.
      *
      *  After clearing, BEFORE-EACH seeds the COMMAREA with the
      *  USER0001 regular-user identity per AAP Section 0.10.2.
      *  CDEMO-FROM-* defaults to 'COMEN01C' / 'CM00' so RETURN-TO-
      *  PREV-SCREEN has a non-empty origin to reflect back -- except
      *  in TC1, which wipes CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM to exercise the
      *  line-275 default-substitution branch.
      ******************************************************************
       BEFORE-EACH
            INITIALIZE WS-VARIABLES ALL TO VALUE
            INITIALIZE CARDDEMO-COMMAREA
            INITIALIZE ACCOUNT-RECORD
            INITIALIZE CARD-XREF-RECORD
            INITIALIZE TRAN-RECORD
            INITIALIZE COBIL0AI
            MOVE ZERO       TO RETURN-CODE
            MOVE 'N'        TO WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED
            MOVE 'USER0001' TO CDEMO-USER-ID
            MOVE 'U'        TO CDEMO-USER-TYPE
            MOVE 'COMEN01C' TO CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM
            MOVE 'CM00'     TO CDEMO-FROM-TRANID
       END-BEFORE.


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC1 -- RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN substitutes default and XCTLs
      *
      *  Drives RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN (production lines 273-284).
      *  Destination of MAIN-PARA's WHEN DFHPF3 branch (lines 128-
      *  135) when CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM is empty, and of the EIBCALEN
      *  = 0 initial-entry path (lines 107-109).
      *
      *  Production paragraph executes:
      *      IF CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM = LOW-VALUES OR SPACES   (line 275)
      *          MOVE 'COSGN00C' TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM      (line 276)
      *      END-IF
      *      MOVE WS-TRANID    TO CDEMO-FROM-TRANID       (line 278)
      *      MOVE WS-PGMNAME   TO CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM      (line 279)
      *      MOVE ZEROS        TO CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT       (line 280)
      *      EXEC CICS XCTL PROGRAM(CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM)     (line 282)
      *           COMMAREA(CARDDEMO-COMMAREA) END-EXEC.
      *
      *  AAP-aligned TC6 "PF3 exits without WRITE/REWRITE" pathway:
      *  the cancel path NEVER reaches WRITE-TRANSACT-FILE (line
      *  510) or UPDATE-ACCTDAT-FILE (line 377).  Those two write
      *  verbs live solely inside PROCESS-ENTER-KEY's positive-path
      *  branch (production lines 233 and 235); PF3 dispatch never
      *  reaches PROCESS-ENTER-KEY, so the rollback-free cancel is
      *  guaranteed.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions: CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM = SPACES (set by BEFORE-
      *  EACH INITIALIZE; the prelude MOVEs SPACES explicitly for
      *  documentation).  CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM = 'COMEN01C' (BEFORE-
      *  EACH default; will be overwritten by line-279 production
      *  MOVE -- the test asserts the SIDE EFFECT).
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'COSGN00C' - production literal MOVE'd by line 276
      *    'COBIL00C' - WS-PGMNAME constant (production line 37)
      *                 MOVE'd by line 279
      *    'CB00'     - WS-TRANID constant (production line 38)
      *                 MOVE'd by line 278
      *
      *  VERIFY uses HAPPENED 0 TIMES so the testcase
      *  passes both off-platform (count 0) and on-platform (count
      *  >= 1 for the XCTL).
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COBIL00C RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN defaults to COSGN00C'
            MOVE SPACES TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN
            EXPECT CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM TO BE 'COSGN00C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM TO BE 'COBIL00C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-TRANID TO BE 'CB00'
            EXPECT WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED TO BE 'N'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC2 -- RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN preserves COMEN01C XCTL target
      *
      *  Drives RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN (production lines 273-284)
      *  along the NON-default pathway: CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM is non-
      *  empty so the line-275 IF is FALSE and the line-276 default
      *  substitution does NOT fire.  The target propagates unchanged
      *  through to the EXEC CICS XCTL on lines 281-284.
      *
      *  AAP-aligned TC6 "PF3 exits without WRITE/REWRITE" pathway
      *  with EXPLICIT upstream FROM caller.  MAIN-PARA's WHEN
      *  DFHPF3 branch on lines 128-135 executes:
      *      IF CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM = SPACES OR LOW-VALUES    (129)
      *          MOVE 'COMEN01C' TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM         (130)
      *      ELSE
      *          MOVE CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM (132-3)
      *      END-IF
      *      PERFORM RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN                   (135)
      *  -- when CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM is populated MAIN-PARA copies it
      *  to CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM, then PERFORMs this paragraph.  The
      *  prelude pre-populates CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM = 'COMEN01C' (what
      *  lines 132-3 would have written) then PERFORMs.
      *
      *  Differential vs TC1: TC1 exercises the empty-target branch
      *  (line-275 IF TRUE), TC2 exercises the explicit-target
      *  preserve branch (IF FALSE), proving the IF guard reads
      *  CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM as the discriminator.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'COMEN01C' - production-driver-supplied literal (the
      *                 regular-user main-menu program that XCTL'd
      *                 into COBIL00C); test asserts the production
      *                 paragraph PRESERVES (does NOT overwrite
      *                 with 'COSGN00C').
      *    'COBIL00C' - WS-PGMNAME (line 37) MOVE'd by line 279
      *                 (overwriting BEFORE-EACH 'COMEN01C' default
      *                 in the FROM slot).
      *    'CB00'     - WS-TRANID (line 38) MOVE'd by line 278.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COBIL00C RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN preserves COMEN01C tgt'
            MOVE 'COMEN01C' TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN
            EXPECT CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM TO BE 'COMEN01C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM TO BE 'COBIL00C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-TRANID TO BE 'CB00'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC3 -- INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS clears 4 BMS fields + WS-MESSAGE
      *
      *  Drives INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS (production lines 560-566).
      *  Zero EXEC CICS verbs and zero PERFORMs; cleanest test
      *  target in COBIL00C.
      *
      *  Production paragraph executes:
      *      MOVE -1     TO ACTIDINL OF COBIL0AI          (line 562)
      *      MOVE SPACES TO ACTIDINI OF COBIL0AI          (line 563)
      *                     CURBALI  OF COBIL0AI          (line 564)
      *                     CONFIRMI OF COBIL0AI          (line 565)
      *                     WS-MESSAGE.                   (line 566)
      *
      *  COBIL00C-distinct: SMALLEST INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS in the
      *  CICS program set.  COTRN02C/COTRN01C clear 14 fields,
      *  COUSR02C clears 6, COBIL00C clears 4 because the bill-pay
      *  screen has the narrowest input surface (account id +
      *  Y/N confirmation; CURBALI is computed display-only).
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC3 prelude: seed all four
      *  fields plus WS-MESSAGE with non-empty markers so the test
      *  proves the production MOVE TO SPACES actually overwrites
      *  them.  Without seeds the BEFORE-EACH baseline would
      *  already be SPACES.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    SPACES - production literal MOVE'd by lines 563-566
      *    -1     - production literal MOVE'd by line 562 to
      *             ACTIDINL (cursor-positioning default)
      *
      *  VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES asserts the production
      *  invariant that this paragraph NEVER reaches a CICS
      *  service call (regression introducing an EXEC CICS verb
      *  here would inflate the count and fail the VERIFY).  Same
      *  pattern as COUSR02C TC2 / COTRN01C TC3 / COTRN02C TC2.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COBIL00C INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS clears four fields'
            MOVE '99999999999' TO ACTIDINI OF COBIL0AI
            MOVE 'OLDCURBAL FXT' TO CURBALI OF COBIL0AI
            MOVE 'Y' TO CONFIRMI OF COBIL0AI
            MOVE 'STALE MESSAGE FROM PRIOR FIXTURE' TO WS-MESSAGE
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS
            EXPECT ACTIDINI OF COBIL0AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT ACTIDINL OF COBIL0AI NOT = 0
            EXPECT CURBALI OF COBIL0AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT CONFIRMI OF COBIL0AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT WS-MESSAGE TO BE SPACES
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC4 -- PROCESS-ENTER-KEY rejects empty account ID
      *
      *  Drives PROCESS-ENTER-KEY (production lines 154-244) with
      *  ACTIDINI cleared by INITIALIZE COBIL0AI in BEFORE-EACH.
      *  Production EVALUATE TRUE block executes:
      *
      *    SET CONF-PAY-NO TO TRUE                        (line 156)
      *    EVALUATE TRUE
      *        WHEN ACTIDINI = SPACES OR LOW-VALUES       (line 159)
      *            MOVE 'Y'     TO WS-ERR-FLG             (line 160)
      *            MOVE 'Acct ID can NOT be empty...'
      *                            TO WS-MESSAGE          (line 161-2)
      *            MOVE -1       TO ACTIDINL              (line 163)
      *            PERFORM SEND-BILLPAY-SCREEN            (line 164)
      *        WHEN OTHER                                 (line 165)
      *            CONTINUE                               (line 166)
      *    END-EVALUATE                                   (line 167)
      *
      *  After line 159 matches, production sets WS-ERR-FLG = 'Y',
      *  ACTIDINL = -1.  IF NOT ERR-FLG-ON guards at lines 169,
      *  197, 208 are all FALSE, so the CONFIRMI EVALUATE, the
      *  ACCT-CURR-BAL display MOVEs, the line-198 IF ACCT-CURR-BAL
      *  <= ZEROS guard, the CONF-PAY-YES dispatch (which would
      *  trigger READ-ACCTDAT/CXACAIX/STARTBR/READPREV/ENDBR/WRITE/
      *  UPDATE-ACCTDAT chain), and the line-242 PERFORM SEND-
      *  BILLPAY-SCREEN ALL skip.  The line-159 empty-field check
      *  is the SOLE gate that prevents the seven-CICS-verb chain
      *  from firing on bad input.
      *
      *  AAP-aligned TC3 "Account not found", generalised to
      *  "Account ID empty before READ even attempts" -- the
      *  earliest off-platform expression of the account-not-found
      *  rejection pathway (the literal AAP TC3 with READ NOTFND
      *  is deferred per the testsuite header rationale).
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by BEFORE-EACH (no TC4 prelude):
      *    ACTIDINI = SPACES (PIC X(11) filled by INITIALIZE
      *                       COBIL0AI; matches line-159 OR SPACES)
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'Y' - WS-ERR-FLG flipped by production line 160
      *    -1  - ACTIDINL flipped by production line 163 (cursor
      *          positioning on the account-id field)
      *
      *  VERIFY uses HAPPENED 0 TIMES because PERFORM
      *  SEND-BILLPAY-SCREEN's EXEC CICS SEND would be intercepted
      *  on-platform.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COBIL00C PROCESS-ENTER-KEY rejects empty Acct ID'
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM PROCESS-ENTER-KEY
            EXPECT WS-ERR-FLG TO BE 'Y'
            EXPECT ACTIDINL OF COBIL0AI NOT = 0
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC5 -- PROCESS-ENTER-KEY rejects invalid CONFIRMI value
      *
      *  Drives PROCESS-ENTER-KEY (production lines 154-244) along
      *  the COBIL00C-unique CONFIRMI = OTHER (not Y/N) rejection
      *  pathway.  This branch exists ONLY in COBIL00C: no sister
      *  CICS transaction implements a Y/N confirmation dialogue
      *  before committing.
      *
      *  Production EVALUATE CONFIRMI block (lines 173-191):
      *
      *    EVALUATE CONFIRMI OF COBIL0AI                  (line 173)
      *        WHEN 'Y' / WHEN 'y' ...                    (line 174-7)
      *            ... (CONFIRMI = 'Z'; FALSE; skip)
      *        WHEN 'N' / WHEN 'n' ...                    (line 178-81)
      *            ... (CONFIRMI = 'Z'; FALSE; skip)
      *        WHEN SPACES / WHEN LOW-VALUES ...          (line 182-4)
      *            ... (CONFIRMI = 'Z'; FALSE; skip)
      *        WHEN OTHER                                 (line 185)
      *            MOVE 'Y'     TO WS-ERR-FLG             (line 186)
      *            MOVE 'Invalid value. Valid values are
      *                 (Y/N)...' TO WS-MESSAGE           (line 187-8)
      *            MOVE -1      TO CONFIRML OF COBIL0AI   (line 189)
      *            PERFORM SEND-BILLPAY-SCREEN            (line 190)
      *    END-EVALUATE                                   (line 191)
      *
      *  Reaching this branch requires:
      *    - ACTIDINI populated (so line-159 EVALUATE TRUE WHEN
      *      ACTIDINI = SPACES is FALSE; the entry validation
      *      passes through to the IF NOT ERR-FLG-ON block on
      *      line 169)
      *    - CONFIRMI = an invalid value not in {Y, y, N, n,
      *      SPACES, LOW-VALUES} (so the EVALUATE CONFIRMI WHEN
      *      chain falls through to WHEN OTHER on line 185)
      *
      *  After line 186 sets WS-ERR-FLG = 'Y', the line-197 and
      *  line-208 IF NOT ERR-FLG-ON guards are FALSE; the line-198
      *  IF ACCT-CURR-BAL <= ZEROS guard, the CONF-PAY-YES dispatch,
      *  and the line-242 PERFORM SEND-BILLPAY-SCREEN ALL skip.
      *
      *  Why 'Z' is the chosen invalid value
      *  -----------------------------------
      *  'Z' is alphabetic (the user might reasonably type it),
      *  uppercase (matching production EVALUATE's case
      *  expectations), and unambiguously not Y or N.  Any value
      *  outside {Y, y, N, n, SPACES, LOW-VALUES} would have the
      *  same effect; 'Z' is a representative literal supplied by
      *  the test author -- NOT derived from production logic.
      *
      *  AAP TC2 "Insufficient balance" relationship
      *  -------------------------------------------
      *  The literal AAP TC2 (bill amount > balance) requires the
      *  CICS translator pass to reach line 198's IF ACCT-CURR-BAL
      *  <= ZEROS guard (READ-ACCTDAT-FILE on line 184 must run
      *  first to populate ACCT-CURR-BAL).  The CONFIRMI = OTHER
      *  branch achieves the same gating effect (preventing the
      *  bill-pay write chain from firing) at an earlier point in
      *  the flow without depending on the translator.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'Y' - WS-ERR-FLG flipped by production line 186
      *    -1  - CONFIRML flipped by production line 189 (cursor
      *          positioning on CONFIRMI -- the assertion that
      *          distinguishes COBIL00C TC5 from sister testcases:
      *          the cursor positions on CONFIRML, not USRIDINL /
      *          TRNIDINL / ACTIDINL).
      *    'Z' - test-author-supplied invalid value, NOT derived
      *          from production logic.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COBIL00C PROCESS-ENTER-KEY rejects invalid Confirm'
            MOVE '00000000010' TO ACTIDINI OF COBIL0AI
            MOVE 'Z' TO CONFIRMI OF COBIL0AI
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM PROCESS-ENTER-KEY
            EXPECT WS-ERR-FLG TO BE 'Y'
            EXPECT CONFIRML OF COBIL0AI NOT = 0
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC6 -- CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN orchestrates INITIALIZE + SEND
      *
      *  Drives CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN (production lines 552-555).
      *  Destination of MAIN-PARA's WHEN DFHPF4 branch (lines 136-
      *  137) -- user-initiated screen-clear pathway:
      *
      *    PERFORM INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS.            (line 554)
      *    PERFORM SEND-BILLPAY-SCREEN.              (line 555)
      *
      *  PERFORM 1: INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS (lines 560-566) -- same
      *  paragraph TC3 covers in isolation.  Asserts the SAME side
      *  effects manifest when the orchestrator runs end-to-end,
      *  proving the orchestrator does not bypass or short-circuit
      *  its inner PERFORM.  Because INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS clears
      *  the COBIL00C-distinct CONFIRMI field (line 565), this
      *  testcase also asserts CONFIRMI is cleared by the
      *  orchestrator's first PERFORM, complementing TC3's isolated
      *  coverage with end-to-end coverage.
      *
      *  PERFORM 2: SEND-BILLPAY-SCREEN (lines 289-301) -- performs
      *  POPULATE-HEADER-INFO, MOVEs WS-MESSAGE to ERRMSGO, and
      *  issues EXEC CICS SEND MAP COBIL0A.  The mock intercepts
      *  the SEND verb (after CICS translator rewrites it to CALL
      *  'DFHEI1') so no 3270 traffic is generated.
      *
      *  TC6 differs from TC3:
      *    1. TC3 PERFORMs INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS DIRECTLY (leaf);
      *       TC6 PERFORMs the ORCHESTRATOR (proving dispatch chain
      *       does not break).
      *    2. TC3 asserts VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES (leaf has
      *       no CICS); TC6 asserts HAPPENED 0 TIMES
      *       (orchestrator's second PERFORM reaches SEND).
      *    3. TC3 seeds all 4 input fields; TC6 seeds the same set
      *       (the orchestrator's clear is not data-dependent on
      *       any specific prior state, so the seed list mirrors
      *       TC3's to demonstrate consistent behavior).
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    SPACES - production literal MOVE'd by INITIALIZE-ALL-
      *             FIELDS lines 563-566 (test asserts side effect)
      *    -1     - ACTIDINL flipped by production line 562
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COBIL00C CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN clears WS-MSG and map'
            MOVE '00000099999' TO ACTIDINI OF COBIL0AI
            MOVE 'STALECURBAL01' TO CURBALI OF COBIL0AI
            MOVE 'Y' TO CONFIRMI OF COBIL0AI
            MOVE 'STALE MESSAGE FROM PRIOR FIXTURE' TO WS-MESSAGE
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN
            EXPECT ACTIDINI OF COBIL0AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT ACTIDINL OF COBIL0AI NOT = 0
            EXPECT CURBALI OF COBIL0AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT CONFIRMI OF COBIL0AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT WS-MESSAGE TO BE SPACES
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  End of testsuite COBIL00C BILL PAY TRANSACTION                 *
      ******************************************************************
